## Eagle Eye W30 (2026-07-26) — Complete ✅

**Files written to `/home/bigpic/projects/bigpic-markets/eagle-eye/W30_2026-07-26/`:**
- `01_equities_sectors.md`, `02_rates_credit_fed.md`, `03_commodities_forex.md`, `04_crypto_alternative.md` — 4 parallel research agents
- `VERIFICATION.md` — cross-checks + spot-checks (**PASS**)
- `EAGLE_EYE.md` — final compiled report

### The two stories
1. **AI-capex trade cracked** — second straight weekly equity loss (S&P -0.6% to 7,411.98, Nasdaq -2.0%, SOX -4.25%). Alphabet's **July 22** beat was *sold hard* on raised capex; Mag 7 shed ~$800B Thursday; TSLA -17.8%. Cybersecurity was the clean rotation-within-tech.
2. **US–Iran war → weekend de-escalation** (the Monday-open lede) — Brent topped $100 intraweek, then strikes paused Sat/Sun, gapping oil ~-5% and lifting Sunday futures (Dow +0.5%, S&P +0.6%, NDX +1.2%). It funnels into a loaded week: FOMC Wed (hold base case but hike odds tripled to ~35–38%), GDP+PCE Thu, and MSFT/META/AAPL/AMZN earnings.

### Verification (6/6 fetchable spot-checks confirmed)
GOOG earnings date/results, Fed hike odds (34.7%, Core PCE 3.4%), Treasury yields (2Y 4.33% / 10Y 4.69%), Brent ($97.04), BTC (~$64.1K), SPX/Nasdaq closes — all confirmed. The "gold bear market" claim reconciled: gold is **-27% from its Jan record ~$5,598** *and* had a +0.96% up-week to ~$4,055 — both true, so I presented the full picture. Two URLs 403/429'd (CNBC, SM Daily Journal) but their figures were independently corroborated.

### One flag worth your attention
`next_week_calendar.md` lists **GOOG earnings for Tuesday, July 28** — but Alphabet **already reported July 22** (verified against 9to5Google + CNBC live coverage). This is the same "stale calendar date" failure mode noted in your existing memory. `stamp-calendar.py` will still inject GOOG under Tuesday's table, so I handled it two ways: treated GOOG as a *recap* item in the Scorecard/narrative, and added a note in the Tuesday commentary that Alphabet has already reported. It's documented in `VERIFICATION.md` in case you want to correct the Calendar API feed upstream.

I did not modify the Week Ahead economic tables — those are left for `stamp-calendar.py` as instructed.
